{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall fill it with stone settings, four rows.</b> And in each row three precious stones, for a court may not have fewer than three, and they would shine like the brilliance of the stones, for the stones of the crown are those whose interior is visible like their exterior. And in the Akedah he wrote that some of these stones were precious and some were cheap, to hint that the judge should regard a lawsuit over a perutah as equal to one of a hundred maneh. And the names of the tribes were engraved upon them according to their birth order, to hint that he must not show favoritism to any person — the small and the great shall he equally heed, as if there is here no advantage for the greatest of the tribes over the smallest of them, but only in the birth order dependent on the years; and apart from this, all are equal. And this is a proper hint. And it also contains a hint to the judge that he must not exalt himself and say, 'I shall rule,' for one whose heart is coarse in halakhic ruling is an ignorant wicked man and arrogant of spirit, and Scripture says (Psalms 25:9), ״יַדְרֵךְ עֲנָוִים בַּמִּשְׁפָּט״ ('He guides the humble in justice'). And the reason for this matter we explained above in parashat Mishpatim. And this is what they said (Shabbat 139a) that in the merit of ״וְרָאֲךָ וְשָׂמַח בְּלִבּוֹ״ ('and he shall see you and rejoice in his heart'), Aharon merited the breastplate of judgment upon the heart — for in the merit of the great humility within him, such that he was not jealous of the authority of Moshe his younger brother in the birth order, he merited the breastplate of judgment, which depends on the quality of humility; and the tribes were written there according to their birth order — and this is measure for measure, literally."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:00.805747883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}